{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":3220856,"duration_api_ms":3226178,"num_turns":43,"result":"All file write operations in this session require user approval in the Claude Code UI. The permission dialog has appeared multiple times but hasn't been approved yet. \n\nHere is the complete WDD YAML content. Please save it to the output path manually, or approve the file write permission when prompted:\n\n**Output path:** `/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_wdd/1000genome-wdd-claude-trial3.yaml`\n\n```yaml\nschema_version: \"wrd-7.0\"\n\nmetadata:\n  workflow_lineage_id: \"wrd:1000genome\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  workflow_name: \"1000genome\"\n  source_format: \"compiled_from_pegasus_dax\"\n  source_file: \"daxgen.py\"\n  generated_by: \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n  generation_date: \"2026-03-04\"\n  workflow_description: >\n    Population genomics workflow processing VCF files from the 1000 Genomes Project.\n    Extracts per-individual mutations per chromosome chunk, merges chunks into per-chromosome\n    archives, annotates variants with SIFT pathogenicity scores from VEP annotation VCFs,\n    then performs pairwise mutation overlap analysis and Monte Carlo allele frequency analysis\n    across 2504 individuals spanning 26 populations.\n  source_repository: \"workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow\"\n  source_commit: \"unknown\"\n  notes: >\n    Static analysis of Pegasus DAX generator (daxgen.py) and five Python task scripts\n    in bin/. Decaf in-memory MPI dataflow alternative (lib/ C++ code) identified but not\n    analyzed in depth; Pegasus path used as primary. Chunk count per chromosome is a\n    runtime parameter in daxgen.py and is not captured here.\n\nstages:\n  - stage_id: \"stage:individuals_processing\"\n    stage_name: \"Individuals Processing\"\n    order: 1\n    description: >\n      Parse VCF files per chromosome chunk and extract per-individual mutation data,\n      producing per-chunk tar.gz archives containing one file per individual.\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    stage_name: \"Merge and Sifting\"\n    order: 2\n    description: >\n      Merge chunked individual archives into per-chromosome tarballs (fan-in), and\n      concurrently extract SIFT pathogenicity scores from VEP annotation VCFs.\n      Both sub-tasks are independent and run in parallel within this stage.\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      - \"task:sifting\"\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    stage_name: \"Population Analysis\"\n    order: 3\n    description: >\n      Consume merged archives and sifted score files to perform pairwise mutation\n      overlap analysis and Monte Carlo allele frequency analysis across populations.\n    tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n\ntasks:\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals\"\n    task_name: \"individuals\"\n    stage_id: \"stage:individuals_processing\"\n    description: >\n      Parses a VCF file line-by-line for a chromosome chunk (a non-overlapping line range),\n      extracts allele calls for all 2504 individuals using a columns mapping file, writes\n      one text file per individual, then compresses all individual files into a tar.gz archive.\n    script: \"bin/individuals.py\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      notes: >\n        One Pegasus job per (chromosome, chunk) pair; chunks are non-overlapping line ranges\n        defined by daxgen.py. Typically 10 chromosomes with N chunks each (N is a runtime\n        parameter). All chunk jobs are independent.\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:chromosome_vcf\"\n      - \"data:columns_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:individual_chr_tar\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Writes 2504 individual text files to a temporary directory per chunk before\n      compressing to tar.gz. This creates significant small-file I/O pressure on\n      shared filesystems (metadata operations dominate). The compress-then-merge\n      pattern results in double serialization before downstream consumption.\n\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    task_name: \"individuals_merge\"\n    stage_id: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Merges all chunked per-chromosome tar.gz archives (fan-in) into a single\n      per-chromosome tarball containing complete per-individual mutation lists\n      across all line ranges for that chromosome.\n    script: \"bin/individuals_merge.py\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      notes: >\n        One Pegasus job per chromosome; all chunk archives for a chromosome must be\n        complete (via Pegasus dependency) before the merge job for that chromosome starts.\n        Independent across chromosomes.\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:individual_chr_tar\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chr_tar\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Extracts all chunk tarballs and re-compresses into a single per-chromosome archive.\n      Intermediate decompressed state can temporarily exceed the final output size on disk.\n      The re-compression step is I/O intensive and could be avoided with streaming approaches.\n\n  - task_id: \"task:sifting\"\n    task_name: \"sifting\"\n    stage_id: \"stage:merge_and_sifting\"\n    description: >\n      Extracts SIFT pathogenicity scores from VEP-annotated VCF files using subprocess\n      grep for fast line filtering followed by Python regex parsing. Produces one text\n      file per chromosome with SIFT-scored variant records.\n    script: \"bin/sifting.py\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      notes: >\n        One Pegasus job per chromosome annotation VCF; entirely independent of the\n        individuals processing path. Runs concurrently with task:individuals_merge\n        within stage:merge_and_sifting.\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:annotation_vcf\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_file\"\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Uses subprocess grep for fast line pre-filtering before Python regex; the grep\n      subprocess call introduces a process-spawn overhead per VCF line batch. Output\n      is a structured text file of SIFT-scored variants per chromosome.\n\n  - task_id: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    task_name: \"mutation_overlap\"\n    stage_id: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    description: >\n      Performs O(N^2) pairwise mutation set intersection analysis across all individuals\n      and population groups. Reads merged chromosome archives and sifted score files,\n      computes overlap statistics, and generates matplotlib plots.\n    script: \"bin/mutation_overlap.py\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"serial\"\n      notes: >\n        Single Pegasus job consuming all 10 merged chromosome archives and 10 sifted\n        chromosome files; O(N^2) over 2504 individuals (approximately 3.1 million pairs).\n        No internal parallelism observed in static analysis.\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chr_tar\"\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_file\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_results\"\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Reads all 10 merged archives into memory for pairwise comparison; memory footprint\n      scales with number_of_individuals * chromosomes * average_mutation_set_size.\n      Matplotlib plot generation adds a CPU+I/O tail to the compute phase.\n\n  - task_id: \"task:frequency\"\n    task_name: \"frequency\"\n    stage_id: \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    description: >\n      Performs 1000 Monte Carlo iterations, sampling 52 random individuals per run\n      to estimate allele frequency distributions across populations using merged\n      chromosome archives and SIFT score files.\n    script: \"bin/frequency.py\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      notes: >\n        1000 independent Monte Carlo runs are logically parallelizable, but the reference\n        implementation in bin/frequency.py runs them serially. Pegasus submits this as a\n        single job. Could be split into 1000 independent tasks for HPC scheduling.\n    io_dominance: \"compute_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chr_tar\"\n      - \"data:sifted_chr_file\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:frequency_results\"\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      CPU-dominant due to 1000 Monte Carlo iterations with random sampling; reads data\n      once at startup then operates primarily in-memory per iteration. The 1000-run\n      loop dominates wall time over I/O activity.\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: \"data:chromosome_vcf\"\n    data_name: \"Chromosome VCF\"\n    description: >\n      Input VCF files from the 1000 Genomes Project; one file per chromosome containing\n      approximately 250,000 SNP records across 2504 individual columns.\n    format: \"vcf\"\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    cardinality: \"10 files (chromosomes 21, 22, and others defined in data.csv)\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n    lifecycle: \"Available before workflow starts; read-only; retained after workflow completes.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:columns_file\"\n    data_name: \"Columns File\"\n    description: >\n      Text file mapping VCF column indices to the 2504 individual identifiers.\n    format: \"text\"\n    category: \"config\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    cardinality: \"1 file\"\n    data_volume_class: \"small\"\n    lifecycle: \"Static configuration input; read-only throughout workflow.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:annotation_vcf\"\n    data_name: \"Annotation VCF\"\n    description: >\n      VEP-annotated VCF files with SIFT pathogenicity predictions per variant; one file\n      per chromosome. Used as input for SIFT score extraction.\n    format: \"vcf\"\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    cardinality: \"10 files (one per chromosome)\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n    lifecycle: \"Available before workflow starts; read-only; retained after workflow completes.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:population_file\"\n    data_name: \"Population File\"\n    description: >\n      Text files listing individual IDs per population group (ALL=2504, AFR=661, AMR=347,\n      EAS=504, EUR=503, GBR=91, SAS=489).\n    format: \"text\"\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    cardinality: \"7 files (one per population group)\"\n    data_volume_class: \"small\"\n    lifecycle: \"Available before workflow starts; read-only; retained after workflow completes.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:individual_chr_tar\"\n    data_name: \"Individual Chromosome Tar\"\n    description: >\n      Per-chromosome-chunk tar.gz archive containing one text file per individual (2504 files)\n      with mutation calls for that chunk.\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"stage_scoped\"\n    cardinality: \"N_chunks * 10 files (chunk count is a runtime parameter)\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n    lifecycle: >\n      Created by task:individuals per (chromosome, chunk) job; consumed by\n      task:individuals_merge; can be deleted after merge completes per chromosome.\n\n  - data_id: \"data:merged_chr_tar\"\n    data_name: \"Merged Chromosome Tar\"\n    description: >\n      Complete per-chromosome tar.gz archive containing one text file per individual\n      (2504 files) with all mutations across all chunks for that chromosome.\n    format: \"tar.gz\"\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    cardinality: \"10 files (one per chromosome)\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n    lifecycle: >\n      Created by task:individuals_merge; consumed by both task:mutation_overlap and\n      task:frequency; retained until workflow completes.\n\n  - data_id: \"data:sifted_chr_file\"\n    data_name: \"Sifted Chromosome File\"\n    description: >\n      Per-chromosome text file of SIFT-scored variants extracted from VEP annotation VCFs.\n    format: \"text\"\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    cardinality: \"10 files (one per chromosome)\"\n    data_volume_class: \"medium\"\n    lifecycle: >\n      Created by task:sifting; consumed by both task:mutation_overlap and task:frequency;\n      retained until workflow completes.\n\n  - data_id: \"data:mutation_overlap_results\"\n    data_name: \"Mutation Overlap Results\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise mutation overlap statistics and matplotlib plots for all individual pairs\n      across populations.\n    format: \"mixed (text statistics + png plots)\"\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    cardinality: \"variable (statistics files + plot images per population)\"\n    data_volume_class: \"medium\"\n    lifecycle: \"Created by task:mutation_overlap; final output; retained indefinitely.\"\n\n  - data_id: \"data:frequency_results\"\n    data_name: \"Frequency Results\"\n    description: >\n      Allele frequency distribution estimates from 1000 Monte Carlo iterations,\n      52 individuals sampled per run.\n    format: \"text\"\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    cardinality: \"1 summary output file\"\n    data_volume_class: \"small\"\n    lifecycle